.TH LALBURST_CUT "1" "January 2026" "LALBurst" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lalburst_cut \- Removes sngl_burst events from XML files according to a variety of criteria.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lalburst_cut.py
[\fI\,options\/\fR] [\fI\,file \/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes sngl_burst events from XML files according to a variety of criteria.
Files named on the command line are read one\-by\-one, and over\-written with the
new files.  If no files are named on the command line, input is read from
stdin and written to stdout.  Note that, for the most part, this program does
not understand coincidence information, and so if an injection or burst event
is removed that participates in a coincidence, this program simply deletes the
entire coincidence as well (before applying the \fB\-\-coinc\-only\fR cut).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-coinc\-only\fR
Discard events that are not participating in a
coincident event.
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR=\fI\,text\/\fR
Set the comment string to be recorded in the process
table for this job (default = None).
.TP
\fB\-\-inj\-made\-only\fR
Discard injections outside the search summary out
segments.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-amplitude\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events below the given amplitude.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-amplitude\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events above the given amplitude.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-bandwidth\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events narrower than the given bandwidth.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-bandwidth\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events wider than the given bandwidth.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-central\-freq\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events with central frequency lower than that
given.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-central\-freq\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events with central frequency higher than that
given.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-confidence\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events below the given confidence.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-confidence\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events above the given confidence.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-duration\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events shorter than the given duration.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-duration\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events longer than the given duration.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-fhigh\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events with highest frequency below the given
frequency.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-fhigh\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events with highest frequency above the given
frequency.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-flow\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events with lowest frequency below the given
frequency.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-flow\fR=\fI\,Hz\/\fR
Discard events with loest frequency above the given
frequency.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-hrss\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events with h_rss below the given value.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-hrss\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events with h_rss above the given value.
.TP
\fB\-\-cut\-instrument\fR=\fI\,name\/\fR
Discard events from given instrument.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-peak\-time\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events with peak time before the given GPS
time.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-peak\-time\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events with peak time after the given GPS
time.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-start\-time\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events starting before the given GPS time.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-start\-time\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events starting after the given GPS time.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-stop\-time\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events ending before the given GPS time.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-stop\-time\fR=\fI\,seconds\/\fR
Discard events ending after the given GPS time.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-snr\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events below the given SNR.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-snr\fR=\fI\,value\/\fR
Discard events above the given SNR.
.TP
\fB\-\-program\fR=\fI\,name\/\fR
Process events generated by the given program.
.TP
\fB\-\-veto\-file\fR=\fI\,filename\/\fR
Veto events using the veto segment list extracted from
this XML file.  The file must contain segment tables,
and the veto list will be constructed from the
segments named "sngl_burst_veto".
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Be verbose.
